```

With the fixed code:

```java
shuffled = {1, 3, 2, 4, 5}
```

So the key fix is:

```java
if (n % 2 == 1) {
    result[n - 1] = nums[n - 1];
}
```

This handles the one leftover element when the array has an odd length.

